"Insertion sort: worst case Θ(n²), best case Θ(n). Any comparison-based sorting problem needs Ω(n log n) comparisons, so merge sort (Θ(n log n)) is asymptotically optimal.",
["Upper bound O(g): running time never exceeds g (for large n).","Lower bound Ω(g): running time is at least g.","Tight bound Θ(g): both.","Bounds can describe an algorithm or a problem.","Problem lower bound: comparison sorting is Ω(n log n).","An algorithm matching the problem's lower bound is optimal."],
["Algorithm bound vs problem bound.","Comparison-sort lower bound.","Optimal algorithm."],
